<title>USA: S&amp;P upgrades Oregon G.O.s to AA - state officials.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P upgrades Oregon G.O.s to AA - state officials.</headline>
<dateline>PORTLAND, Ore. 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's Corp has upgraded Oregon's general obligation bond rating from AA-minus to AA, citing the state's improved economy, officials with the Oregon state Treasury said on Monday.</p>
<p>S&amp;P said an announcement would be made shortly.  </p>
<p>In addition, the rating agency said the outlook was now stable, according to Michael Parker, spokesman for state Treasurer Jim Hill.</p>
<p>&quot;We're very excited about this,&quot; said Parker. &quot;The economy has really boosted our efforts.&quot;</p>
<p>Hill plans to hold a press conference Tuesday to discuss the rating upgrade, Parker said.</p>
